for your interest LSU New Orleans Department of Chemistry graduate program! You can begin your application process by submitting an application to LSU New Orleans Graduate School.\nGraduate Record Exam (GRE) scores are not required by LSU New Orleans Department of Chemistry.\nSupplementary materials are required for M.S. and Ph.D. applicants and should be uploaded directly through your application.\nA current r\u00e9sum\u00e9 or C.V.\nAt least three letters of recommendation are required for entrance into the Ph.D. program and two for the M.S. program.\nA statement of purpose explaining your interest in graduate school and if you are interested in a specific area of chemistry. Please indicate if you are undecided.\nSubmission of materials through your application is required, unless you obtain departmental permission for alternative submission.\nStart Your Application\nNext Steps\nFinancial Support\nApply to LSU New Orleans\nResources\nGraduate School\nGraduate School Forms\nGraduate School Requirements for International Students\nGraduate Record Exam (GRE)\nContact\nDr. Viktor Poltavets ([email protected])\nFooter\nContact\n2000 Lakeshore Drive New Orleans, LA 70148\n[email protected]\n[email protected]\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (504) 384-7924\n+1 (504) 384-7924\nLearn\nAdmission information\nPrograms of study\nScholarships and awards\nTuition and fees\nGraduate programs\nFinancial aid\nImportant dates & deadlines\nExperience\nInternational center\nOur campus\nStudent life\nHousing\nCareer services\nAlumni\nMake a gift\nAnnual Security Report\nConnect\nAll social\nUniversity calendar\nNews\nFor parents\nEspanol - Tieng Viet\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nNon-Discrimination\nTitle IX\nCampus Crime\nEmergency Preparedness\n\u00a9 2026 LSU New Orleans. All Rights Reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics/cos/chemistry/graduate/application-process#main"], ["", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/"], ["", "https: